<title>USA: Midwest Cash Grain PM - Weak demand for corn.</title>
<headline>Midwest Cash Grain PM - Weak demand for corn.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corn basis bids were weaker at several locations on Thursday as sluggish demand weighed on the market, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is just no demand for it (corn) at the moment,&quot; one Iowa-based dealer said.</p>
<p>The corn basis weakened at several locations from Evansville, Indiana, to Davenport, Iowa.</p>
<p>&quot;People are loading (rail) cars with nowhere to go,&quot; another dealer said, noting basis bids in Kansas City were around three cents lower at six cents over CBOT July.</p>
<p>Wheat and soybean basis bids were mostly steady.</p>
<p>Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures, cash $/bu.</p>
